00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:29.380
on your heels and lifting
your butt off of the bench.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.030
Some people say that this allows them

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:33.140
to target the lower portion of the chest.

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:36.500
I think that if you want to
do that, do a decline bench.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:39.074
And the fact that he's
wearing those wrist supporters

00:09:39.074 --> 00:09:40.980
at such a lightweight

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.820
tells me that he's
probably benching too much.

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:44.990
You can't allow one part of your body

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:46.510
to become overdeveloped

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:48.230
and think that everything
is gonna be okay.

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:49.810
You are bound to have an injury.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.150
If your wrists are not strong
enough to hold the weight

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.910
and you have to put
something artificially here.

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:55.730
This is not, I'm not talking
about like strong men

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:57.260
or like these extreme weights.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.400
As an average lifter,

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.360
it means you best be
working on those wrists

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:01.560
instead of using that.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:02.870
And lower the weight a little.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:05.300
What's harder, med school or law school?

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:06.470
We debate it right here

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:07.820
with the LegalEagle.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.060
Click here to check that out.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.603
As always, stay happy
and healthy in the gym.

00:10:12.726 --> 00:10:14.491
(man grunts)

00:10:14.491 --> 00:10:17.074
(upbeat music)

